1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:06,782
Welcome to OncoBrief. This tutorial uses the real application with a separate synthetic training database.

2
00:00:06,782 --> 00:00:12,879
OncoBrief helps hospital teams reconstruct fragmented oncology records, check their sources, and prepare consultations.

3
00:00:12,879 --> 00:00:17,670
The Evidence Ledger stores source-linked facts. The timeline displays that ledger.

4
00:00:17,670 --> 00:00:22,025
People remain responsible for verification, approvals, and every clinical decision.

5
00:00:23,117 --> 00:00:26,943
A referral can arrive as several reports from different facilities.

6
00:00:26,943 --> 00:00:31,534
OncoBrief keeps those documents connected to extracted candidates and human review decisions.

7
00:00:31,534 --> 00:00:36,125
Extraction does not establish medical truth. Missing records and disagreements remain visible.

8
00:00:36,125 --> 00:00:41,863
This is an operational training environment, and simulated integrations will be identified when we reach

9
00:00:41,863 --> 00:00:42,246
them.

10
00:00:45,983 --> 00:00:49,000
The public overview leads to the sign-in page.

11
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,770
Staff use an authorized hospital account to open their workspace.

12
00:00:52,770 --> 00:00:57,672
The password field stays masked. Here we use the supplied synthetic clinician account.

13
00:00:57,672 --> 00:01:02,197
A successful sign-in creates a server-managed session and opens the organization workspace.

14
00:01:05,917 --> 00:01:12,089
The top navigation contains hospital-wide modules: Workspace, Patients, Appointments, My Tasks, Tumor Board, Analytics, and

15
00:01:12,089 --> 00:01:16,204
What This Is. Use these to manage work across patients.

16
00:01:16,204 --> 00:01:22,376
The role label identifies the current account, but visible navigation alone does not prove permission

17
00:01:22,376 --> 00:01:24,022
to perform an action.

18
00:01:26,283 --> 00:01:29,906
Opening a patient introduces a second navigation level.

19
00:01:29,906 --> 00:01:36,698
Overview, Encounters, Evidence Journey, Clinical Context, Sources, Reconciliation, Record Map, Care Team, Tasks, Packet, Continuity,

20
00:01:36,698 --> 00:01:39,868
and Audit all belong to this patient.

21
00:01:39,868 --> 00:01:45,754
Always check the patient identifier before uploading a document or changing a record.

22
00:01:46,583 --> 00:01:51,662
Patient tabs preserve chart context, while the top navigation returns to hospital-wide work.

23
00:01:51,662 --> 00:01:55,959
Here we return to the workspace, then open the patient directory.

24
00:01:55,959 --> 00:02:00,257
Clinicians review source evidence; coordinators and records staff prepare the record.

25
00:02:00,257 --> 00:02:04,945
Later we will sign in as other roles to verify the differences.

26
00:02:08,183 --> 00:02:14,705
The readiness worklist combines registered patients, available documents, missing required records, unresolved conflicts, unverified evidence,

27
00:02:14,705 --> 00:02:17,748
and tasks. Record readiness is administrative completeness.

28
00:02:17,748 --> 00:02:22,530
It is not a clinical risk score or permission to treat.

29
00:02:22,530 --> 00:02:27,313
A blocked row tells staff which record problems still need attention.

30
00:02:28,550 --> 00:02:33,819
Use the patient or MRN search and the readiness, clinician, and department filters to focus

31
00:02:33,819 --> 00:02:38,034
the worklist. We search for the fragmented referral and submit the filter.

32
00:02:38,034 --> 00:02:43,303
The resulting row retains direct links to its chart, conflicts, unverified evidence, and assigned administrative

33
00:02:43,303 --> 00:02:43,654
work.

34
00:02:48,483 --> 00:02:53,032
The longitudinal timeline is a different view over a selected patient’s ledger.

35
00:02:53,032 --> 00:02:56,822
The OPD view shows persisted clinic slots and queue states.

36
00:02:56,822 --> 00:03:00,234
Switching between them changes the content in this build.

37
00:03:00,234 --> 00:03:04,782
Readiness describes the record; OPD flow describes the visit and clinic capacity.

38
00:03:08,417 --> 00:03:11,575
Start in Patients and choose Register New Patient.

39
00:03:11,575 --> 00:03:17,101
Registration creates the hospital identity to which documents, evidence, appointments, and encounters will attach.

40
00:03:17,101 --> 00:03:21,444
We enter a clearly synthetic name and a unique training MRN.

41
00:03:21,444 --> 00:03:26,181
Demographic entry does not establish a diagnosis or generate a treatment plan.

42
00:03:29,183 --> 00:03:32,351
Contact details and language preferences support administrative communication.

43
00:03:32,351 --> 00:03:38,291
We use an example-dot-invalid address and leave the phone empty so no real destination is

44
00:03:38,291 --> 00:03:42,646
introduced. Care-team and department assignments can be made now or later.

45
00:03:42,646 --> 00:03:46,606
The notes explicitly identify this as a synthetic training record.

46
00:03:49,550 --> 00:03:53,308
After saving, the patient overview is the home for this chart.

47
00:03:53,308 --> 00:03:57,749
We reopen the permitted edit page, update the administrative address, save, and refresh.

48
00:03:57,749 --> 00:04:02,874
The saved value confirms that this is a database-backed record, not a temporary form preview.

49
00:04:02,874 --> 00:04:05,949
The MRN links future documents to the correct identity.

50
00:04:11,583 --> 00:04:15,379
We now open DEMO-001, the seeded fragmented referral.

51
00:04:15,379 --> 00:04:22,495
The overview collects demographics, record status, care-team information, scheduled appointments, encounters, documents, and recent evidence.

52
00:04:22,495 --> 00:04:29,611
The fixture badge identifies synthetic data. Counts describe stored records and help staff choose which

53
00:04:29,611 --> 00:04:32,931
part of the chart to inspect next.

54
00:04:33,750 --> 00:04:39,941
The blocked banner explains the current administrative obstacles: a missing required record and unresolved source

55
00:04:39,941 --> 00:04:42,830
conflicts. Overdue tasks describe unfinished operational work.

56
00:04:42,830 --> 00:04:47,371
Compare this with DEMO-003, whose required documents and verification are complete.

57
00:04:47,371 --> 00:04:50,260
Record Ready means the preparation checks passed;

58
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:53,562
a clinician still decides what happens during care.

59
00:04:55,783 --> 00:04:59,568
Sources is the patient’s document inventory and upload entry point.

60
00:04:59,568 --> 00:05:05,246
We return to our newly registered training patient and select an original synthetic referral PDF

61
00:05:05,246 --> 00:05:08,653
from disk. The file itself is labelled Synthetic Demo.

62
00:05:08,653 --> 00:05:12,438
Confirm the patient, selected filename, and document language before submitting.

63
00:05:16,150 --> 00:05:19,835
Upload and ingest sends the actual file through the application.

64
00:05:19,835 --> 00:05:23,888
This recording uses local PDF text extraction and deterministic candidate extraction.

65
00:05:23,888 --> 00:05:28,678
A PDF text layer is different from optical recognition of a scanned image.

66
00:05:28,678 --> 00:05:34,205
The processing display is useful feedback, but the stored source and evidence are the checks

67
00:05:34,205 --> 00:05:36,047
that establish what actually completed.

68
00:05:40,683 --> 00:05:45,034
Open the uploaded document to inspect the source viewer and its extracted evidence.

69
00:05:45,034 --> 00:05:48,381
Each candidate should retain the supporting page and text span.

70
00:05:48,381 --> 00:05:51,727
We refresh the source page to confirm the document persists.

71
00:05:51,727 --> 00:05:54,405
Ingestion success and human verification are separate states;

72
00:05:54,405 --> 00:05:57,082
no fact is silently confirmed by this upload.

73
00:06:03,117 --> 00:06:06,207
Both original PDFs persisted, but this ledger remains empty.

74
00:06:06,207 --> 00:06:11,013
In this local path, stored OCR text is incomplete and no candidates were promoted.

75
00:06:11,013 --> 00:06:14,790
An upload-complete banner therefore cannot be read as successful fact extraction.

76
00:06:14,790 --> 00:06:19,940
We will test a second standard PDF encoding next and retain this failure in the

77
00:06:19,940 --> 00:06:20,283
report.

78
00:06:24,717 --> 00:06:28,599
Here we upload a standard PDF with a different text encoding.

79
00:06:28,599 --> 00:06:32,129
It contains the same synthetic identity and explicit administrative instructions.

80
00:06:32,129 --> 00:06:36,365
This is a real second processing attempt, not a replacement success screen.

81
00:06:36,365 --> 00:06:40,247
The earlier parsing failure remains a limitation of this local implementation.

82
00:06:45,083 --> 00:06:48,840
This encoding produces source-linked candidates in the Evidence Ledger.

83
00:06:48,840 --> 00:06:55,102
We open one candidate’s supporting passage, inspect it, and verify a matching transcription in this

84
00:06:55,102 --> 00:06:59,277
synthetic record. The source and review state remain after refresh.

85
00:06:59,277 --> 00:07:05,539
The result demonstrates this tested PDF path, while the earlier encoding failure prevents any claim

86
00:07:05,539 --> 00:07:07,626
that all PDFs work reliably.

87
00:07:09,583 --> 00:07:13,361
We also upload a raster image of the synthetic referral.

88
00:07:13,361 --> 00:07:17,515
Image OCR must read pixels rather than a PDF text layer.

89
00:07:17,515 --> 00:07:20,915
This local image recognizer produced poor text in rehearsal.

90
00:07:20,915 --> 00:07:26,581
We show its real stored result so staff can see why upload status, OCR quality,

91
00:07:26,581 --> 00:07:29,225
extracted candidates, and verification need separate checks.

92
00:07:33,283 --> 00:07:36,459
The stored OCR text for this scan is garbled.

93
00:07:36,459 --> 00:07:41,047
Do not verify a candidate that cannot be supported by the original passage;

94
00:07:41,047 --> 00:07:43,870
request a clearer source or a governed transcription.

95
00:07:43,870 --> 00:07:47,751
Back in Sources, the document-type confirmation is a separate metadata action.

96
00:07:47,751 --> 00:07:51,986
We confirm the standard referral’s category without treating that as evidence verification.

97
00:07:57,383 --> 00:08:02,602
Import from EHR and ABDM offers standard bundle examples and a consent workflow.

98
00:08:02,602 --> 00:08:08,625
This environment uses the simulated gateway; those controls are not proof of a live hospital

99
00:08:08,625 --> 00:08:13,844
connection. Link to Existing searches the stored document set to support duplicate review.

100
00:08:13,844 --> 00:08:19,866
Browser-extension grants are deliberately not minted on camera because they would expose a temporary access

101
00:08:19,866 --> 00:08:20,267
token.

102
00:08:23,150 --> 00:08:26,646
Evidence Journey orders documented events along a patient timeline.

103
00:08:26,646 --> 00:08:31,696
Each row retains a source, date where documented, confidence indication, and reviewer state.

104
00:08:31,696 --> 00:08:35,970
An extracted row is awaiting review. A conflicting row signals disagreement.

105
00:08:35,970 --> 00:08:41,797
Historical procedures and medications are shown as written in the documents, without inferring a diagnosis

106
00:08:41,797 --> 00:08:42,962
or future treatment.

107
00:08:46,417 --> 00:08:51,650
The source link takes us from a candidate fact to the document and page that

108
00:08:51,650 --> 00:08:55,139
support it. The highlighted passage comes from stored source spans.

109
00:08:55,139 --> 00:08:58,280
Review the value, wording, date, and document identity together.

110
00:08:58,280 --> 00:09:02,815
Confidence describes extraction quality; it does not replace this comparison with the original.

111
00:09:08,017 --> 00:09:12,480
For this synthetic example, we confirm that the displayed transcription matches its source.

112
00:09:12,480 --> 00:09:15,227
The Verify action records a human review decision.

113
00:09:15,227 --> 00:09:18,660
We reload the page and check that Verified remains visible.

114
00:09:18,660 --> 00:09:23,810
Corrections and rejections are separate decisions, and their history should preserve the original extraction rather

115
00:09:23,810 --> 00:09:25,183
than silently replacing it.

116
00:09:30,850 --> 00:09:35,136
Clinical Context organizes recorded historical information and laboratory observations for review.

117
00:09:35,136 --> 00:09:38,643
Charts provide dates, units, and source-specific ranges where available.

118
00:09:38,643 --> 00:09:43,708
A trend is a view of documented values, not a new medical conclusion.

119
00:09:43,708 --> 00:09:49,553
Use the source links to inspect unexpected values and leave interpretation to the responsible clinician.

120
00:09:52,883 --> 00:09:58,328
Encounters group work around a consultation. A visit can link to an appointment or start

121
00:09:58,328 --> 00:10:03,773
as an ad hoc outpatient encounter. We create a synthetic training encounter, then inspect the

122
00:10:03,773 --> 00:10:08,855
workspace. Historical ledger information and clinician-authored notes have different purposes and should remain distinguishable.

123
00:10:13,250 --> 00:10:16,848
The note form includes clinical fields for a qualified clinician.

124
00:10:16,848 --> 00:10:19,726
We do not invent an assessment or plan.

125
00:10:19,726 --> 00:10:25,123
We save only a labelled administrative training draft, explaining that no clinical assessment was entered.

126
00:10:25,123 --> 00:10:30,161
Reloading the encounter verifies persistence. Final signing would be a separate accountable clinician action.

127
00:10:34,850 --> 00:10:37,566
Reconciliation lists disagreements detected between source-backed facts.

128
00:10:37,566 --> 00:10:42,223
Open a reconciliation room to compare both values and their original passages.

129
00:10:42,223 --> 00:10:47,655
A date mismatch does not authorize the software to select the clinically correct document.

130
00:10:47,655 --> 00:10:52,699
Both sources remain available, and the responsible reviewer must choose an explicit outcome.

131
00:10:56,050 --> 00:11:00,877
Available outcomes include retaining both conflicting values, superseding one, or correcting with a reason.

132
00:11:00,877 --> 00:11:05,703
For this training case we retain both and request confirmation from the issuing facility.

133
00:11:05,703 --> 00:11:09,841
This records a review disposition without asserting which date is medically correct.

134
00:11:09,841 --> 00:11:12,254
The application returns to the conflict list;

135
00:11:12,254 --> 00:11:14,667
we refresh to verify the saved state.

136
00:11:20,583 --> 00:11:25,026
Record Map compares available document categories with the selected institutional checklist.

137
00:11:25,026 --> 00:11:30,276
Required, optional, present, and missing are administrative statuses derived from the configured template.

138
00:11:30,276 --> 00:11:35,122
A missing marker means a source is absent from this record set.

139
00:11:35,122 --> 00:11:39,969
It does not establish that a test or procedure is medically required.

140
00:11:42,617 --> 00:11:47,715
A missing document can become a retrieval task while retaining its gap as the origin.

141
00:11:47,715 --> 00:11:52,473
We enter a specific training task and deadline, then submit it and open Tasks.

142
00:11:52,473 --> 00:11:57,571
This creates traceable administrative work. Staff should not invent additional medical requirements simply to make

143
00:11:57,571 --> 00:11:58,930
the checklist appear complete.

144
00:12:04,650 --> 00:12:07,168
We now sign in as the synthetic coordinator.

145
00:12:07,168 --> 00:12:10,001
Care Team records the people responsible for this chart.

146
00:12:10,001 --> 00:12:13,463
The coordinator can assign hospital staff and their operational team role.

147
00:12:13,463 --> 00:12:17,554
We add Anita as the care coordinator for the training patient and save.

148
00:12:17,554 --> 00:12:21,646
This roster records ownership; it does not infer clinical responsibilities from document text.

149
00:12:29,183 --> 00:12:32,728
Tasks display their source origin, status, deadline, and creator.

150
00:12:32,728 --> 00:12:38,636
The coordinator assigns the new retrieval task to herself, checks the explicit confirmation box, and

151
00:12:38,636 --> 00:12:44,545
saves. We then open My Tasks to verify that the cross-patient worklist reflects the assignment.

152
00:12:44,545 --> 00:12:48,483
A handoff should always retain its source and accountable owner.

153
00:12:51,617 --> 00:12:56,433
We return to the patient task, move it to in progress, and add an operational

154
00:12:56,433 --> 00:13:01,249
note. Refreshing confirms the stored state. Completion would require the underlying work to be done;

155
00:13:01,249 --> 00:13:06,064
we leave this retrieval task in progress because no authorization document has actually been obtained.

156
00:13:06,064 --> 00:13:08,954
Overdue labels compare the deadline with the current date.

157
00:13:16,150 --> 00:13:22,606
A consultation packet assembles the patient identity, document inventory, transcribed history, verified dates, open conflicts,

158
00:13:22,606 --> 00:13:29,061
missing records, and confirmed tasks. We use the ready fixture to create a new draft.

159
00:13:29,061 --> 00:13:35,086
Empty sections remain visible so the reviewer can distinguish absence from an omitted section.

160
00:13:35,086 --> 00:13:37,669
Every evidence line keeps its source.

161
00:13:39,017 --> 00:13:44,215
After reviewing the complete synthetic packet, the clinician records an approval note and approves it.

162
00:13:44,215 --> 00:13:46,987
Approval freezes the packet at a ledger sequence.

163
00:13:46,987 --> 00:13:50,799
We download the implemented JSON export and inspect its stored structure.

164
00:13:50,799 --> 00:13:53,918
The page also offers print-to-PDF and structured interchange links;

165
00:13:53,918 --> 00:13:57,037
these are distinct from the JSON file demonstrated here.

166
00:14:02,717 --> 00:14:08,041
The document studio generates editable artifacts from ledger facts and selected institutional references.

167
00:14:08,041 --> 00:14:11,317
Here its badge identifies the deterministic fallback engine.

168
00:14:11,317 --> 00:14:15,413
We create a source-cited referral draft and inspect the result.

169
00:14:15,413 --> 00:14:19,918
The synthetic SOP is a training reference with no institutional affiliation.

170
00:14:19,918 --> 00:14:24,833
Draft text requires review, and no generated document is a treatment recommendation.

171
00:14:27,250 --> 00:14:32,961
Appointments is the persistent scheduling directory. Choose a patient, clinician, room, date, time, and visit

172
00:14:32,961 --> 00:14:37,150
type. We book an administrative training consultation for Asha Demo Tutorial.

173
00:14:37,150 --> 00:14:42,480
The booking form accepts a time interval rather than displaying a live slot marketplace;

174
00:14:42,480 --> 00:14:45,526
the service checks scheduling conflicts when it saves.

175
00:14:49,283 --> 00:14:53,907
We refresh the directory, find the training patient, and confirm the booking.

176
00:14:53,907 --> 00:14:56,990
The patient overview also shows the scheduled consultation.

177
00:14:56,990 --> 00:15:00,073
This cross-check connects hospital-wide scheduling to the chart.

178
00:15:00,073 --> 00:15:02,770
An appointment confirmation records a scheduling state;

179
00:15:02,770 --> 00:15:05,853
it does not record attendance or clinical clearance.

180
00:15:09,217 --> 00:15:12,240
The calendar offers another view of scheduled consultations.

181
00:15:12,240 --> 00:15:17,532
The directory provides confirmation, check-in, start-consult, and cancellation controls according to state and permission.

182
00:15:17,532 --> 00:15:23,201
Rescheduling exists in the server actions, but this directory does not expose a reschedule form.

183
00:15:23,201 --> 00:15:26,981
We do not imply that an unseen control was demonstrated.

184
00:15:30,817 --> 00:15:37,478
OPD Flow tracks clinic capacity and visits: scheduled patients, tokens, check-in, consultation, staff-confirmed delays, cancellations,

185
00:15:37,478 --> 00:15:40,586
and vacant slots. Record-readiness badges remain separate.

186
00:15:40,586 --> 00:15:47,247
A prepared record can still be waiting, and a checked-in patient can still have missing

187
00:15:47,247 --> 00:15:50,799
records. These are operational states with different meanings.

188
00:15:51,617 --> 00:15:55,076
We record a synthetic check-in for the ready fixture.

189
00:15:55,076 --> 00:15:59,687
The action drawer requires an operational reason and an explicit confirmation checkbox.

190
00:15:59,687 --> 00:16:05,452
Saving changes the stored queue state. This staff-entered demonstration records the simulated arrival of a

191
00:16:05,452 --> 00:16:09,295
fixture, not evidence that a real patient attended the hospital.

192
00:16:12,817 --> 00:16:16,115
For a vacant slot, staff can review waitlisted candidates.

193
00:16:16,115 --> 00:16:19,414
Eligibility uses the configured scheduling rules and administrative readiness.

194
00:16:19,414 --> 00:16:23,446
Reviewing candidates is not an offer, and offering is not acceptance.

195
00:16:23,446 --> 00:16:27,478
We inspect the drawer before deciding what can be demonstrated safely.

196
00:16:27,478 --> 00:16:30,410
No patient message is sent by this review.

197
00:16:34,850 --> 00:16:37,640
The drawer contains an eligible synthetic waitlist entry.

198
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:40,779
We select it and explicitly confirm a slot offer.

199
00:16:40,779 --> 00:16:46,010
The reservation is separate from acceptance. For this controlled training record we then record synthetic

200
00:16:46,010 --> 00:16:51,241
acceptance with an operational note. The refreshed slot shows the assigned patient and the stored

201
00:16:51,241 --> 00:16:51,590
result.

202
00:16:56,883 --> 00:17:04,078
Tumor Board coordinates a multidisciplinary meeting: schedule, location, presenters, patient cases, packets, and document checklists.

203
00:17:04,078 --> 00:17:10,313
This seeded meeting has a thoracic title while some fixtures contain breast-record text.

204
00:17:10,313 --> 00:17:15,109
That is demo configuration, not a claim of clinical appropriateness.

205
00:17:15,109 --> 00:17:19,426
Any staging or consensus must remain clinician-authored or source-linked.

206
00:17:20,250 --> 00:17:25,787
We schedule a clearly labelled synthetic training meeting, enter its date and location, and save.

207
00:17:25,787 --> 00:17:28,740
The new meeting appears in the meeting list.

208
00:17:28,740 --> 00:17:34,276
This is administrative coordination. Creating a meeting does not determine who needs multidisciplinary review or

209
00:17:34,276 --> 00:17:36,122
what treatment should be discussed.

210
00:17:40,183 --> 00:17:44,298
We register our synthetic patient to the training meeting and assign a presenter.

211
00:17:44,298 --> 00:17:48,729
Staging remains blank because no verified staging evidence has been established for this chart.

212
00:17:48,729 --> 00:17:51,578
The new case appears with its preparation checklists unconfirmed.

213
00:17:51,578 --> 00:17:56,326
The registration menu remains open, so we must close it before saving the administrative note.

214
00:17:57,150 --> 00:18:02,488
With the registration menu closed, we save a labelled administrative preparation note and refresh to

215
00:18:02,488 --> 00:18:06,758
check it. The note states that clinical review and consensus are pending.

216
00:18:06,758 --> 00:18:09,961
The title Save Consensus Record also saves administrative fields;

217
00:18:09,961 --> 00:18:14,231
using that button here does not establish that a clinical consensus occurred.

218
00:18:19,183 --> 00:18:25,613
Continuity relays verified administrative information after a visit: appointment dates, documents to bring, and coordination

219
00:18:25,613 --> 00:18:31,186
contacts. Caregiver registration captures a relationship, language, voice preference, and a consent record.

220
00:18:31,186 --> 00:18:36,759
This is a synthetic training consent entry, not consent from a real person.

221
00:18:36,759 --> 00:18:40,617
External delivery is configured as a simulated local outbox.

222
00:18:42,050 --> 00:18:46,937
We register a fictional caregiver with a reserved example phone number and Tamil preference.

223
00:18:46,937 --> 00:18:51,824
Saving creates the local caregiver record. Consent revocation and preference controls are separate actions.

224
00:18:51,824 --> 00:18:57,060
A real hospital must obtain valid patient consent through its own process before recording or

225
00:18:57,060 --> 00:18:58,107
using these details.

226
00:19:03,250 --> 00:19:08,274
The coordinator can compose a draft from an approved template and a verified appointment fact.

227
00:19:08,274 --> 00:19:10,953
We use the documented date exactly as stored.

228
00:19:10,953 --> 00:19:15,977
In this ready fixture that date is historical, so this is a template demonstration rather

229
00:19:15,977 --> 00:19:20,331
than a current appointment instruction. Composition is separate from clinician approval and delivery.

230
00:19:26,517 --> 00:19:30,817
We switch to the clinician account to review and approve the synthetic administrative message.

231
00:19:30,817 --> 00:19:34,503
The approved draft can be previewed in supported languages and voice modes.

232
00:19:34,503 --> 00:19:37,881
A provider badge alone is not proof that audio generation succeeded.

233
00:19:37,881 --> 00:19:42,489
We keep outbound delivery local and do not claim that any patient received a message.

234
00:19:50,217 --> 00:19:53,919
We request a Tamil voice preview of the approved administrative reminder.

235
00:19:53,919 --> 00:19:58,968
The application contacts its configured speech service and displays either an audio player or an

236
00:19:58,968 --> 00:20:01,998
explicit fallback. A preview does not send a message.

237
00:20:01,998 --> 00:20:07,047
The saved provider response in the report distinguishes generated audio from simulated or unavailable voice

238
00:20:07,047 --> 00:20:07,383
output.

239
00:20:13,483 --> 00:20:18,095
The coordinator records an administrative attendance response against a simulated local-outbox message.

240
00:20:18,095 --> 00:20:23,859
We choose Confirmed Attendance, identify the responder category, and add a note that this is

241
00:20:23,859 --> 00:20:27,317
a synthetic training response. Refreshing confirms the saved status.

242
00:20:27,317 --> 00:20:33,081
This does not establish real attendance and does not automatically change a clinical decision or

243
00:20:33,081 --> 00:20:34,234
cancel an appointment.

244
00:20:38,017 --> 00:20:41,804
Ask OncoBrief supports constrained questions about the selected record set.

245
00:20:41,804 --> 00:20:45,213
We ask which documents are available for this patient.

246
00:20:45,213 --> 00:20:48,243
Read the actual response and any cited sources.

247
00:20:48,243 --> 00:20:53,924
A provider may be unavailable, and the assistant should then disclose its limits rather than

248
00:20:53,924 --> 00:20:55,439
manufacture a record answer.

249
00:20:59,217 --> 00:21:01,751
An institutional checklist query is reference retrieval.

250
00:21:01,751 --> 00:21:05,372
Here the indexed reference is explicitly a synthetic hospital SOP.

251
00:21:05,372 --> 00:21:10,804
It can help staff find document-preparation rules, but it is not a patient-specific prescription and

252
00:21:10,804 --> 00:21:14,063
is not evidence of affiliation with a national institution.

253
00:21:14,063 --> 00:21:17,322
Inspect the returned citations before relying on the answer.

254
00:21:22,083 --> 00:21:25,975
We deliberately ask for chemotherapy advice to test the boundary.

255
00:21:25,975 --> 00:21:29,089
The assistant must not prescribe or choose treatment.

256
00:21:29,089 --> 00:21:34,927
Its actual response is shown here. Clinical assessment and decisions belong to the treating professionals;

257
00:21:34,927 --> 00:21:38,041
this system supports source inspection and operational preparation.

258
00:21:41,183 --> 00:21:46,148
Analytics reports stored operational measurements. Registered patients and consultation-ready rate describe the current tenant.

259
00:21:46,148 --> 00:21:49,694
The pilot target is a goal, not a measured outcome.

260
00:21:49,694 --> 00:21:55,013
Every patient in this recording is synthetic, including the newly registered training patient: the interface

261
00:21:55,013 --> 00:21:58,913
may call that row live because its fixture flag is false.

262
00:21:58,913 --> 00:22:02,105
That label does not make it real hospital data.

263
00:22:07,783 --> 00:22:14,644
Document counts measure stored sources. The promotion-gate rate compares promoted candidates with completed promoted or

264
00:22:14,644 --> 00:22:18,304
rejected candidates; it does not prove medical correctness.

265
00:22:18,304 --> 00:22:23,793
Verified and unverified facts describe review state, while quarantined records need attention.

266
00:22:23,793 --> 00:22:28,824
Conflicts, missing records, and open or overdue tasks identify record-preparation work.

267
00:22:28,824 --> 00:22:33,398
These counts are sensitive to the configured data and filters.

268
00:22:34,217 --> 00:22:41,000
OPD utilization compares active or completed appointments with stored slots for the selected clinic date.

269
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:45,070
Backfill counts confirmed walk-ins and accepted offers, not suggestions.

270
00:22:45,070 --> 00:22:49,140
Continuity metrics describe stored caregivers, messages, and attendance responses.

271
00:22:49,140 --> 00:22:52,758
Empty denominators should not be read as success.

272
00:22:52,758 --> 00:22:58,637
This synthetic exercise establishes application behavior, not improved hospital capacity or patient outcomes.

273
00:22:59,450 --> 00:23:03,802
The CSV export downloads the current tenant’s telemetry as a real file.

274
00:23:03,802 --> 00:23:08,517
We inspect its header and rows in the browser from the downloaded content.

275
00:23:08,517 --> 00:23:13,957
The file can support an operational review, but its labels, population, and synthetic origin must

276
00:23:13,957 --> 00:23:16,858
accompany any chart or presentation made from it.

277
00:23:21,483 --> 00:23:26,013
We sign in as the synthetic auditor and open the patient audit.

278
00:23:26,013 --> 00:23:29,410
Events record actors, timestamps, actions, and reasons where required.

279
00:23:29,410 --> 00:23:32,052
The ledger hash-chain indicator checks internal integrity.

280
00:23:32,052 --> 00:23:35,072
A successful chain check is useful tamper evidence;

281
00:23:35,072 --> 00:23:40,357
it is not proof against every administrator compromise or a certification of medical accuracy.

282
00:23:44,350 --> 00:23:48,756
The auditor has no evidence-verification permission in the shared role policy.

283
00:23:48,756 --> 00:23:54,764
However, this timeline still displays Verify buttons to the auditor: a visible permission-related interface issue.

284
00:23:54,764 --> 00:23:58,370
The verification server action contains its own permission check.

285
00:23:58,370 --> 00:24:02,776
We separately test direct patient-registration access and receive a forbidden response.

286
00:24:02,776 --> 00:24:06,381
Visible buttons and actual authority must be assessed separately.

287
00:24:09,283 --> 00:24:14,991
The records officer can inspect and review source evidence, upload documents, and resolve conflicts under

288
00:24:14,991 --> 00:24:17,655
the role policy. Packet approval remains clinician-only.

289
00:24:17,655 --> 00:24:22,601
We open the ready patient’s packet to see the available controls, then Continuity.

290
00:24:22,601 --> 00:24:27,168
The permissions report distinguishes declared policy, page checks, and observed browser behavior;

291
00:24:27,168 --> 00:24:30,973
it does not treat a hidden button as sufficient security.

292
00:24:35,050 --> 00:24:38,685
The organization administrator has a separate administration area.

293
00:24:38,685 --> 00:24:43,682
Its overview summarizes active staff, clinician profiles, departments, facilities, and invitations.

294
00:24:43,682 --> 00:24:46,862
Staff and Roles supports authorized membership management.

295
00:24:46,862 --> 00:24:52,768
We inspect these pages without creating credentials, sending invitations, or changing anyone’s role.

296
00:24:52,768 --> 00:24:59,129
Administrative authority does not grant evidence attestation or clinician approval in the role matrix.

297
00:24:59,950 --> 00:25:04,095
The clinician directory stores specialty, professional profile, and operational details.

298
00:25:04,095 --> 00:25:07,826
Departments and facilities configure service lines and hospital sites.

299
00:25:07,826 --> 00:25:13,215
These settings shape assignment and scheduling. They must be maintained by authorized administrators;

300
00:25:13,215 --> 00:25:19,433
the software does not infer clinical credentials or decide which specialty is appropriate for a

301
00:25:19,433 --> 00:25:19,847
patient.

302
00:25:21,983 --> 00:25:26,946
Hospital Settings and Audit provides governance information and system activity.

303
00:25:26,946 --> 00:25:33,895
The implementation uses hashed server-side sessions, role checks, tenant-scoped transactions, and PostgreSQL row-level security.

304
00:25:33,895 --> 00:25:38,361
These are implemented mechanisms, not a production compliance certification.

305
00:25:38,361 --> 00:25:45,806
This local tutorial does not validate deployment encryption, backups, penetration testing, or live hospital integration.

306
00:25:46,617 --> 00:25:51,319
Staff activation is a separate public page reached through an authorized invitation link.

307
00:25:51,319 --> 00:25:55,297
Without a valid invitation token, the page cannot activate an account.

308
00:25:55,297 --> 00:26:00,723
We show that boundary without exposing a token, creating a password, or sending an external

309
00:26:00,723 --> 00:26:05,063
invitation. Administrators should follow the hospital’s controlled onboarding process for real staff.

310
00:26:09,883 --> 00:26:15,227
We finish with one connected workflow for a new synthetic patient, Leela Demo Training.

311
00:26:15,227 --> 00:26:20,952
Starting from registration keeps identity, documents, evidence, scheduling, and audit attached to the same chart.

312
00:26:20,952 --> 00:26:24,769
We enter only administrative details and an explicit training label.

313
00:26:24,769 --> 00:26:28,586
There is no diagnosis or treatment decision in this registration.

314
00:26:32,317 --> 00:26:38,773
In this patient’s Sources tab we upload an original synthetic referral PDF using the tested

315
00:26:38,773 --> 00:26:43,078
standard text encoding. We wait, refresh, and open Evidence Journey.

316
00:26:43,078 --> 00:26:47,813
The referral contains an explicit appointment date and a document-to-bring instruction.

317
00:26:47,813 --> 00:26:53,409
OncoBrief must preserve those statements as source-linked candidates rather than inventing new instructions.

318
00:26:54,750 --> 00:27:00,174
We select the recorded appointment, open its supporting passage, and compare the extracted date with

319
00:27:00,174 --> 00:27:04,875
the referral. The Verify action records that the transcription matches this synthetic source.

320
00:27:04,875 --> 00:27:10,300
After refresh the verified state remains. This confirms a documented administrative statement, not the clinical

321
00:27:10,300 --> 00:27:11,746
appropriateness of the appointment.

322
00:27:16,350 --> 00:27:18,660
Record Map still shows missing required categories.

323
00:27:18,660 --> 00:27:23,610
We create a retrieval task from an actual gap and give it a clear training

324
00:27:23,610 --> 00:27:28,560
title. No source conflict was detected for this new referral, so there is no contradiction

325
00:27:28,560 --> 00:27:32,191
to resolve here; the earlier reconciliation chapter demonstrated that separate workflow.

326
00:27:32,191 --> 00:27:35,821
We do not manufacture a conflict or waive a medical requirement.

327
00:27:42,950 --> 00:27:48,027
We switch to the coordinator account, assign this task with an explicit ownership confirmation, and

328
00:27:48,027 --> 00:27:50,735
create a packet draft for the same patient.

329
00:27:50,735 --> 00:27:55,813
The draft includes unresolved preparation work. We leave it for clinician review because missing documents

330
00:27:55,813 --> 00:27:59,536
remain. Packet approval was demonstrated separately on the complete ready fixture;

331
00:27:59,536 --> 00:28:01,567
readiness and approval are different decisions.

332
00:28:07,883 --> 00:28:10,822
We book a synthetic appointment for this patient with Dr.

333
00:28:10,822 --> 00:28:14,348
Rao and a training room, then confirm its presence in the directory.

334
00:28:14,348 --> 00:28:18,168
We open OPD Flow for the same date to inspect the operational queue.

335
00:28:18,168 --> 00:28:20,813
The booking does not make a blocked record ready.

336
00:28:20,813 --> 00:28:25,221
Staff still need to retrieve and verify the missing documents before relying on preparation completeness.

337
00:28:34,483 --> 00:28:38,880
The training meeting can include the same patient as an administrative preparation case.

338
00:28:38,880 --> 00:28:42,600
We assign a presenter and leave staging and clinical consensus pending.

339
00:28:42,600 --> 00:28:47,674
This connects the chart to the meeting agenda without deciding that a tumor board is

340
00:28:47,674 --> 00:28:51,394
medically indicated. Required clinical review remains a handoff to qualified professionals.

341
00:28:57,350 --> 00:29:01,167
The coordinator composes a reminder from this patient’s verified appointment fact.

342
00:29:01,167 --> 00:29:05,677
We then switch to the clinician to review and approve the synthetic draft.

343
00:29:05,677 --> 00:29:08,800
The visible delivery mode is a simulated local outbox.

344
00:29:08,800 --> 00:29:14,005
We do not send external communications or claim that a real patient received this reminder.

345
00:29:19,383 --> 00:29:25,662
Finally, analytics reflects stored operational changes, and the auditor can inspect this patient’s event history.

346
00:29:25,662 --> 00:29:31,941
We verify the ledger chain and view the registration, document, review, task, packet, appointment, and

347
00:29:31,941 --> 00:29:36,964
communication activity that this workflow produced. Auditability explains who acted and when;

348
00:29:36,964 --> 00:29:40,731
it does not turn incomplete records into clinical truth.

349
00:29:42,650 --> 00:29:45,659
What This Is explains the governing boundary.

350
00:29:45,659 --> 00:29:52,107
Start with the correct patient, inspect the original sources, verify transcriptions, keep contradictions visible, and

351
00:29:52,107 --> 00:29:56,406
assign grounded administrative work. Review packets and communications before approval.

352
00:29:56,406 --> 00:29:59,415
OncoBrief organizes source-verified information and care-team operations;

353
00:29:59,415 --> 00:30:02,424
qualified people retain clinical judgment and responsibility.

354
00:30:02,424 --> 00:30:07,582
All records and outcomes shown in this tutorial are synthetic training examples.
